{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmmnCcPRUjwAmj2e9EgE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm 24, I have a salary, and I came here to see how \"my\" fund (the iShares S&P 500 Swap, yearly fee 0.05%) compares with the funds on the list. I left the sliders as they were: 10,000 ₪ now, 500 ₪ a month, 10 years, 7%.\n\n## 1. What I'd do and how sure I am\n\nI'd drop my fund and go with what the page puts on top: an account at **פסגות** (Psagot) with the fund **\"ילין לפידות מחקה S&P 500 (4D)\"**, which ends at **86,492 ₪**.\n\n- **About not buying my fund: about 70% sure.** In the main list, my fund's row only says **\"עוד לא נאסף\"** (not collected yet) and **\"אין מחיר כאן\"** (no price here). It gets no final number. The only number I found for it was further down, in the table **\"סוג קרן אחר, אותו חשבון\"** (another fund type, same account): **59,196 ₪**, marked **\"פחות 19,980 ₪\"** (19,980 less) with a red bar. That is almost 20,000 ₪ less than the Israeli funds, which scared me off. I also noticed my fund costs 0.05% a year, and the Yelin fund shows **0.02%**.\n- **About Psagot + Yelin being right: about 60% sure.** I don't fully trust it. The lower part of the page starts from a different place (**\"עכשיו: MTF סל (S&P 500 (4D)), ירושלים\"**, 79,176 ₪) and I don't know why. The 20,000 gap might also come from the bank, not from my fund. I can't tell.\n\n## 2. What I actually used\n\n- The four boxes at the top (now / monthly / years / return per year).\n- The result card: **\"הבחירה שלכם · הזול\"** (your choice · the cheapest) 86,492 ₪, next to **\"הזוג הבא בתור\"** (the next pair) at −43 ₪.\n- The right-hand list **\"כל החשבונות\"** (all the accounts), mainly the amounts left at the end.\n- The left-hand list **\"כל הקרנות על מדד S&P 500\"** (all the S&P 500 funds), where I found my own fund.\n- The table **\"סוג קרן אחר, אותו חשבון\"**, the only place with a number for my fund.\n\n## 3. Going down the page\n\n1. **Title, index buttons, short S&P 500 text:** Used. I checked that S&P 500 was selected and stopped there.\n2. **The four boxes and sliders:** Used them to read my plan, didn't change anything. Skipped the **\"אינפלציה\"** (inflation) button.\n3. **Result card (86,492 vs 86,449):** Used. It's clear, and a 43 ₪ gap means the top two are basically the same.\n4. **Coloured bar and \"עלות אצלכם, לעומת הזוג הבא השני\"** (your cost, compared with the next pair): Skimmed. \"1 ₪ more / 58 ₪ less / 14 ₪ more\" is too small to matter to me.\n5. **Chosen account and fund cards (Psagot, Yelin):** Used. I saw **\"דמי ניהול 0%\"** (management fee 0%) and was happy.\n6. **Left fund list:** Used the last column and scrolled until I found my fund with the **\"הזנתם\"** (you entered) tag and 0.05%. All the coloured tags confused me.\n7. **Right account list:** Used the amounts and read a few **\"לא בחישוב\"** (not in the calculation) notes. These are discounts for students and soldiers that don't apply to me.\n8. **Interactive Brokers box (82,848 ₪ with a different iShares):** Confused me. Is that how I'd buy my fund? It's a different fund, not mine.\n9. **\"למה חלק מהקרנות בלי מחיר\"** (why some funds have no price): Read part of it. It says the price list has no line for foreign securities. I partly understood why I got no number.\n10. **Advertising versus price lists, \"פסגות · 3 טענות\"** (Psagot · 3 claims): Skimmed. It worried me a bit, since my choice is Psagot and it has 3 claims against what it advertises.\n11. **\"מה הכי משנה את מה שיישאר לכם\"** (what changes your result most), with its chart and table: Skimmed. I took away that years and the monthly amount matter most. I didn't look at the lines.\n12. **\"עם נטרול מט״ח או בלי\"** (with or without currency hedging) and the dollar and year charts: Skipped. I didn't understand it and it didn't feel like my question.\n13. **\"מתחילים מבחירה אחת\"** (start from one choice), the waterfall chart: Confused me. It starts from Jerusalem, which I never chose.\n14. **The two tables at the end:** Used the fund-type one to find my fund. Glanced at the account one.\n15. **Notes at the bottom and the \"חוקים וכללים\"** (rules) link: Skipped.\n\n## 4. Lists, tables and charts\n\n- **Fund list:** I looked at the fund name and the **\"לעומת הבחירה\"** (compared with the choice) column. I ignored **\"מול המדד\"** (against the index, the +0.37% figures) and almost all the coloured tags. I only noticed **\"מס רק במכירה\"** (tax only on sale) and **\"נקנית בחו״ל\"** (bought abroad) on my fund.\n- **Account list:** I looked at the big number (86,492, 83,396 and so on) and the bank name. I didn't understand the small number underneath (1,057, 4,541) or the orange, yellow and red bars.\n- **Last tables:** I looked at **\"נשאר בסוף\"** (left at the end) and **\"עוד/פחות\"** (more/less), and at the green and red bars to see good versus bad. I ignored the **\"יותר כסף/פחות כסף\"** (more/less money) header line.\n- **Line chart and the dollar and hedging charts:** Ignored them, including the colours and years.\n\n## 5. What I didn't understand\n\n- **\"4D\", \"4A\"**, **\"Swap\"**, **\"Acc\"**, and the codes like IE00B5BMR087.\n- **\"מנוטרלת מט״ח\"** (currency-hedged), **\"חשיפה לדולר\"** (dollar exposure), **\"צוברת\"** and **\"חלוקת דיבידנד\"** (accumulates vs. pays dividends), **\"נאמן\"** (trustee), **\"צריך טופס W-8BEN\"** (needs a W-8BEN form).\n- **\"נשען על כלל מס פתוח: מוצג ולא מדורג\"** (relies on an open tax rule: shown but not ranked). Is my 59,196 real or not?\n- Why the bottom part starts from Jerusalem MTF and not from my choice.\n- The small number under each bank in the account list.\n\n## 6. What I wanted to know and couldn't find\n\n- **One final number for my fund at Psagot**, the top choice, next to the 86,492. Can I even buy it there?\n- **Why my fund comes out about 20,000 ₪ lower.** Is it the fund, the bank, or tax?\n- Which accounts let me buy a fund abroad, and what that costs.\n- In plain words: is a foreign fund worth it for someone like me, yes or no?\n\n## 7. If half the page had to go\n\nFirst to go:\n1. The whole **\"עם נטרול מט״ח או בלי\"** section with its dollar charts and year table.\n2. The **\"מה הכי משנה\"** line chart and table.\n3. The waterfall chart.\n4. The advertising-claims list.\n5. Most of the coloured tags on the funds.\n\nI'd keep the sliders, the result card, the two lists, and the table that showed my fund. That table should be much higher up the page, next to my fund."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19996,"cache_read_input_tokens":3723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19996},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25921a54-db07-4352-806d-c42dd404fed5","uuid":"795d355d-84a5-4093-be36-acea74540f39","timestamp":"2026-11-06T13:43:57.567Z","request_id":"req_011CgmmnBgq1nZBTmHqfqwfi"}
